    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Food Online turns WooCommerce products into a restaurant menu where customers browse, choose options and order without leaving the page.</p>\n<p>Build the menu page with the Food Online Menu block, or use the classic shortcodes on any page.</p>\n<h4>Food Online Menu block</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add the menu in the block editor and style it in the block settings.</li>\n<li>Start from a ready-made template: Valdemar Dark, Ellen Noble, Einar&#8217;s Fusion, Arcade, Street or the 2026 Template.</li>\n<li>Product popup with options, mini cart and category navigation.</li>\n<li>Show opening hours and the estimated order time above the menu.</li>\n<li>Works with block themes and classic themes.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Classic shortcodes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>[foodonline] or [foodonline2] shows the full menu with categories, product popup and mini cart.</li>\n<li>[foodonline_menu] and [foodonline_minicart] place the menu and the cart separately, for example in a page builder layout.</li>\n<li>Choose categories, tags, products and order: [foodonline categories=&#8221;pizza,salad&#8221;].</li>\n<li>One column, two columns or the 2020 layout. Choose per page with layout=&#8221;twocols&#8221;.</li>\n<li>Give the classic menu the look of a block template with template=&#8221;arcade&#8221;, and show category images with category_image=&#8221;yes&#8221;.</li>\n<li>Settings for colors, icons, product images, popups, search, sticky category menu, accordion and the mobile bottom bar.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Products</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Use WooCommerce simple and variable products. Attributes give choices such as sizes, toppings and sides.</li>\n<li>Compatible with <a href=\"https://woocommerce.com/products/product-add-ons/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">WooCommerce Product Add-Ons</a>.</li>\n<li>Menu sections follow your WooCommerce product categories and their order.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Works with</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/shipping-zones-by-drawing-for-woocommerce/\" rel=\"ugc\">Shipping Zones by Drawing</a> for delivery areas drawn on a map.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://liveorderconfirmationplugin.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Live Order Confirmation</a> for incoming orders in real time and order approval.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://foodonlineplugin.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Food Online Premium</a>, an optional separate plugin with delivery modes, address validation, pickup locations, time selection and checkout blocks.</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Make sure WooCommerce is installed and active.</li>\n<li>Install and activate Food Online for WooCommerce.</li>\n<li>Add your dishes as WooCommerce products and put them in product categories. The categories become the menu sections.</li>\n<li>Create a menu page:\n<ul>\n<li>Block editor: add the <strong>Food Online Menu</strong> block and choose a template.</li>\n<li>Classic: add the shortcode [foodonline] (or [foodonline2] if your theme changes the WooCommerce product loop).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Classic menu settings are in WooCommerce &gt; Settings &gt; Food Online. The Blocks Guide on the same page explains the block.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<h4>\nBlock or shortcode?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Use the Food Online Menu block on new pages. The shortcodes remain for existing pages and page builders. Both work with block themes and classic themes.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan a page use other settings than the global ones?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. The shortcodes accept template=&#8221;…&#8221;, layout=&#8221;…&#8221; and category_image=&#8221;…&#8221;. The first menu shortcode on the page that sets them decides.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nHow do I change the order of categories and products?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Categories follow the order in WooCommerce &gt; Products &gt; Categories, or the Food Online category sorting. Products follow the WooCommerce menu order, or orderby=&#8221;…&#8221; in the shortcode.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan I offer toppings and side dishes?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, with variable products and attributes, or with WooCommerce Product Add-Ons.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan I define the delivery area with a drawn zone?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, with <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/shipping-zones-by-drawing-for-woocommerce/\" rel=\"ugc\">Shipping Zones by Drawing</a>.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan I translate Food Online?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. Translations are managed on translate.wordpress.org, and you can adjust texts with a plugin such as Loco Translate.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>6.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Major release. Please test on a staging site before updating a live store.</li>\n<li>New: Food Online Menu block with six ready-made templates.</li>\n<li>New: Menu templates for the classic shortcodes, chosen in the settings or with template=&#8221;…&#8221;.</li>\n<li>New: Shortcode attributes layout=&#8221;…&#8221; and category_image=&#8221;…&#8221; for [foodonline], [foodonline2] and [foodonline_menu].</li>\n<li>New: Manual category sorting.</li>\n<li>Changed: Reorganized settings.</li>\n<li>Fix: Shortcode settings are now applied in block themes.</li>\n<li>Fix: Product names with &#8220;&amp;&#8221; in the mini cart.</li>\n<li>Fix: Stray output from bundled files could break REST and AJAX responses.</li>\n<li>Compatibility: WordPress 7.1 and WooCommerce 11.2.</li>\n<li>Requirements: WordPress 6.6 and WooCommerce 9.8 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.6.11</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Prevented a fatal error in WooCommerce&#8217;s New order email preview when it uses an unsaved preview order.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.6.10</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility: Compatible with WooCommerce 9.8 &amp; WordPress 6.8</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.6.9</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility: Compatible with WooCommerce 9 and blocks checkout.</li>\n<li>PHP: Updated compatibility with PHP 8.3.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.6.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Script wc_cart_fragments needs to be manually loaded since WooCommerce 7.8. Conditional checks fixed.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Script wc_cart_fragments needs to be manually loaded since WooCommerce 7.8</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.5</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility: Increased compatibility with Divi page builder</li>\n<li>Compatibility: Compatibility with WooCommerce HPOS (beta)</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.4</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Menu category images</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added: New filters &#8216;fdoe_is_shortcode_topbar&#8217; and &#8216;fdoe_is_shortcode_delivery&#8217;</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New: New option to show a sale badge in the menu</li>\n<li>Added: New filter &#8216;fdoe_is_shortcode_minicart&#8217;</li>\n<li>Fix: Minicart increment buttons don´t work in shortcode &#8216;foodonline_minicart&#8217; for some cases</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.1.14</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New behavior: Product sorting now default to &#8220;menu order&#8221;</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.1.12</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New behavior: Category sorting now default to &#8220;menu order&#8221;</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.1.10</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Improvement: Shortcodes improvement</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.1.7</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility: Compatible with WP 6.1</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.4.1.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New option: Category Menu horitazional scrollable</li>\n<li>Version harmonization</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.3.0.5</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility: Compatible with Live Order Confirmation Plugin</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.3.0.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes: Minor bug fixes and adjustments</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.3.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility: Compatible with Shipping Zones by Drawing 2.7.0</li>\n<li>Fixes: Minor bug fixes and adjustments</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.2.0.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Trailing whitespace may cause incorrect output</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.2.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Ajax nonces</li>\n<li>Improvement: Improved jQuery 3 compatibility</li>\n<li>Improvement: Coding standard improvement</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.1.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Option “Show subcategories together with their parent category and not as an independent category” cause the menu to stop loading</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New feature: Live search in menu</li>\n<li>Improvement: jQuery 3 compatibility</li>\n<li>New behavior: Availability schedule categories and tags now work as an AND condition if both are set for a schedule</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.5</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Remove button in mini cart does not show for some configurations</li>\n<li>Improvment: Improved rtl language support</li>\n<li>Improvment: Uppdated templates &#8216;simple.php&#8217; &amp; &#8216;product-image.php&#8217; for &#8216;single-product&#8217;</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New behavior: Removed stripping html-tags from product short description</li>\n<li>New behavior: Order status &#8216;on-hold&#8217; is now included when counting &#8220;extra time&#8221;</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: CSS fix cart modal</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>MAJOR UPDATE *</li>\n<li>New behavior: If you have schedules with the application “Place Order”, it is now mandatory to choose some product categories to which the schedule applies to</li>\n<li>New feature: New abilities on how to calculate order times</li>\n<li>Fix: Closing tag missing on the shop link element</li>\n<li>New feature: Popup informing on which products that are not available to order according to availability schedules</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Turn your WooCommerce products into a restaurant menu with fast ordering, on desktop and mobile.",
